nch (through C6 but via hydroxyacetone cyanohydrin)\",\n      \"description\": \"Hydroxyacetone branch entering cyanohydrin and C6 aminonitrile, then hydrolysis.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_002\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_003\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Extended DHA branch (through C6 via DHA cyanohydrin)\",\n      \"description\": \"DHA branch entering chain extension and amination to C6 aminonitrile, then final hydrolysis.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_011\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_003\", \"mol_013\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hub_molecules\": [\"mol_003\"],\n  \"convergence_points\": [\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_003\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_008\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}", "parsed_response": {"target_molecule": "L-Valine", "overall_strategy": "Comprehensive cyanosulfidic network for prebiotic L-valine synthesis, integrating all experimentally supported literature routes from C3 sugar derivatives (dihydroxyacetone and hydroxyacetone) in surface cyanosulfidic pools. The network implements full atom/charge-balanced reactions with explicit byproducts (all small molecules accounted for: H2O, H2S, NH3, disulfane), avoiding unsupported speculative direct amination and unbalanced chain-shortening steps. Core sequence uses copper/H2S-mediated reductive deoxygenation, cyanohydrin and thioamide intermediates, copper-catalyzed chain extension, Strecker-type amination, and hydrolysis. Alternative converging routes from both C3 feedstocks and via both C5 and C6 aminonitriles are explicitly included. Ten distinct pathways arise from combinations of upstream feedstock choice, chain extension route, and hydrolysis entry point.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "C3H6O3", "iupac_name": "1,3-dihydroxypropan-2-one", "common_name": "dihydrox